course: dictionary
lesson: 10444
title: Small word, big meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Truly» is an adverb. An adverb adds information to a verb, an adjective or another adverb, often telling how strongly or how honestly something is meant.
explain: «Truly» has three main meanings. It can mean really or sincerely: «I am truly sorry» means the sorry is honest. It can mean very or completely: «a truly amazing day» is amazing all the way through. It can also end a formal letter as «Yours truly».
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the words around it. «Bats are the only mammals that can truly fly» means really fly, not just glide. Swap in really or very, then check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Truly» is an adverb, so it adds to the meaning of a verb, an adjective or another adverb.
fact: «Truly» can mean really or sincerely: «I'm truly sorry» means the apology is honest.
fact: «Truly» can mean very or completely: «a truly magical place» is magical all the way through.
fact: «Yours truly» ends a formal letter, mostly in American English. It can also be a jokey way to say "me".
fact: Phrases with truly include «truly grateful», «really and truly» and «well and truly».
exercise: «I am truly sorry for breaking your pencil.» What does truly mean here? | Not at all | Very quickly | Loudly | *Really and sincerely
exercise: «False alarms make it harder to be believed when it truly matters.» What meaning of truly fits best? | *Really, in a way that counts | Happily | Only once | Quietly
exercise: Which ending is used to finish a formal letter? | *Yours truly | Goodbye forever | Lots of kisses
test: «Bats are the only mammals that can truly fly.» Truly here means: | *Really, in a way that is true | Slowly | Quietly | Happily
test: «It was a truly amazing day.» What does truly mean? | Yesterday | Honestly and sincerely | Sadly | *Very, completely
exam: Which sentence uses truly to mean very or completely? | I am truly sorry | *It was a truly magical place | Yours truly | Are you truly sure?
